  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general business law, in relation to requiring appearance enhancement business owners to provide masks and gloves to nail specialists",
    "basePrintNo": "S8096",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8096-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §404-b, Gen Bus L",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8096\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to requiring\nappearance enhancement business owners to provide masks and gloves to\nnail specialists\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis bill requires nail salon owners and operators of appearance\nenhancement businesses to make available upon request protective masks\nand gloves to their employees. It also gives employees the right to wear\nsuch protection it they so choose,\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nThis bill adds section 404-b to the general business law. § 404-b\nrequires all owners and operators of appearance enhancement businesses\nwhich practice nail specialty shall make available, upon request, gloves\nand face masks for nail speciality licensees who work in such busi-\nnesses.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nIn many nail salons, employees would like to use protective equipment\nsuch as gloves and masks while they work.  However, many owners forbid\nor discourage their workers from doing this as it could potentially\nscare away customers. This can have detrimental effects on the health\nand safety of workers. By requiring owners to make available protective\nequipment and also allow their workers to wear it if they so choose,\nthis will help to protect nail salon workers who spend many hours a day\nin rooms filled with toxic fumes, chemicals and particulate matter.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nOn the one hundred eightieth day after it shall have become law.\n\n",
